# package-lock.json — Locked Dependency Versions

## Layman's terms

A snapshot of the exact versions of every tool the project uses. Ensures everyone (and every deploy) gets the same versions. Don't edit by hand—`npm install` updates it when dependencies change.

## Medium understanding

npm's lockfile. Records the resolved dependency tree from package.json so installs are reproducible. Commit this file so CI and other devs get identical node_modules. Edit package.json for changes; lockfile updates automatically.

## Advanced

- **Generated:** By `npm install` when package.json or deps change
- **Reproducibility:** `npm ci` uses lockfile exclusively for install
- **Do not edit manually**
